title: Key Dates in British History
subject: History
level: KS3
emoji: 🏰
front-template: What happened in {}?
description: Big moments from 1066 to the modern day.
---
1066 :: Norman Conquest – William of Normandy wins the Battle of Hastings.
1215 :: King John seals Magna Carta at Runnymede.
1348 :: The Black Death arrives in England.
1381 :: The Peasants' Revolt, led by Wat Tyler.
1455–1487 :: The Wars of the Roses.
1485 :: Henry Tudor wins the Battle of Bosworth and becomes Henry VII.
1534 :: Act of Supremacy – Henry VIII becomes head of the Church of England.
1588 :: The Spanish Armada is defeated.
1605 :: The Gunpowder Plot.
1642–1651 :: The English Civil War.
1649 :: Charles I is executed.
1666 :: The Great Fire of London.
1707 :: Act of Union joins England and Scotland.
1805 :: Battle of Trafalgar – Nelson defeats the French and Spanish fleets.
1807 :: The slave trade is abolished in the British Empire.
1815 :: Battle of Waterloo – Napoleon defeated.
1832 :: The Great Reform Act extends voting rights.
1837 :: Queen Victoria becomes monarch.
1918 :: Some women get the vote in Britain.
1928 :: Women get equal voting rights with men.
1948 :: The NHS is founded.
1953 :: Elizabeth II is crowned.
1973 :: The UK joins the European Economic Community.
2022 :: Queen Elizabeth II dies; Charles III becomes King.
